## 7. Conclusion

We have presented the ARS model, a rigorous theoretical framework for the cognitive evaluation of artificial intelligence grounded in psychometric factor analysis. The framework defines three latent factors—Alignment, Robustness, and Self‑assessment—with full mathematical formalisation, including normalisation, a safety‑centric geometric composite, closed‑form uncertainty propagation with higher‑order bounds, a synergy index corrected for factor correlations, and a theorem demonstrating the sufficiency of three factors under plausible loading structures. All definitions are accompanied by proofs of boundedness, monotonicity, and statistical guarantees. The entire work is offered as a set of falsifiable theoretical claims, ready for the empirical testing that will transform it into a trustworthy instrument for the safe and transparent assessment of intelligent machines.

