### C.2 Reward Opacity Metric Details

Given a set of reward functions \(\mathcal{R} = \{r_1, \dots, r_m\}\), compute the value \(V_r^\pi = \mathbb{E}_\pi[\sum_t \gamma^t r(s_t,a_t)]\) and the optimal value \(V_r^* = \max_{\pi'} V_r^{\pi'}\). Then opacity is:
\[
\Omega = 1 - \min_{r \in \mathcal{R}} \frac{V_r^\pi}{V_r^*}.
\]
If any \(V_r^* = 0\) (all rewards zero), that \(r\) is excluded. \(\Omega \in [0,1]\); a value close to \(1\) indicates high opacity (system far from any hypothesised objective). This metric is computed via Monte Carlo rollouts or analytical bounds.

